cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "snowreach: virga classification and blind-zone simulation for vertically pointing radars"
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper it comes from."
type: software
license: BSD-3-Clause
version: 1.0.1
abstract: >-
  Two methods for deciding whether the snow a vertically pointing radar
  detects aloft reaches the ground: a classification of the profiles into
  precipitation, virga and noise, and a simulation of the lowest observable
  height of a spaceborne radar, which reports what the blind zone costs in
  occurrence and in accumulated water equivalent.
keywords:
  - virga
  - snowfall
  - Antarctica
  - Micro Rain Radar
  - blind zone
  - CloudSat
  - EarthCARE
authors:
  - family-names: Roversi
    given-names: Giacomo
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6560-2307"
    affiliation: "Ca' Foscari University of Venice, and CNR-ISAC, Rome"
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    Virga hidden within the blind zone of spaceborne radars: implications for
    surface snowfall estimates in coastal East Antarctica
  status: submitted
  journal: "Atmospheric Chemistry and Physics"
  year: 2026
